      "id": 1,
      "text": "Middleburg District was created by Maryland’s General Assembly on March 24, 1852, naming William Shepperd, William Shaw, and John Clabaugh as commissioners to set its boundaries.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.marylandroots.org/index.php/county-resources/carroll-county/93-historyofwesternmaryland/67-middleburg-district-no-10-chapter-39a",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Western Maryland Railroad cuts through Middleburg’s southern side, while the Frederick and Pennsylvania Line Railroad nearly bisects the district, linking it to regional trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.marylandroots.org/index.php/county-resources/carroll-county/93-historyofwesternmaryland/67-middleburg-district-no-10-chapter-39a",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "South of Main Street, the Brooks family once owned dense woods that covered the land in 1800.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.marylandroots.org/index.php/county-resources/carroll-county/93-historyofwesternmaryland/67-middleburg-district-no-10-chapter-39a",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Set against the Blue Ridge Mountains, Middleburg showcases small‑town charm with art museums, historic landmarks, fine cuisine, and unique antiques.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
